175	616,1312,1132,1764	Fig. 175.	The corolla of the Morning-Glory alone, seen obliquely: a broad open funnel with a plain, slightly wavy border, narrowing to a short tube below.
176	792,1785,963,1998	176 Morning-Glory.	The calyx of the Morning-Glory: five separate, narrow, pointed sepals standing up round the base of the flower.
177	1180,976,1680,1990	177 Stramonium.	A Stramonium flower: the long calyx-tube with five short teeth at its top, and the corolla rising out of it as a long tube spreading into five pointed lobes.
